  "explanation": {
    "id": "1b4a103d-d9b6-4af3-9834-6e0b04fae761",
    "body": "Since $\\vec{F}$ is a conservative field, you can use the Fundamental Theorem of Line Integrals, which states that the integral depends only on the endpoints of the curve:$$\\int_{C} \\vec{\\nabla}\\phi \\cdot d\\vec{r} = \\phi(\\vec{r}(2\\pi)) - \\phi(\\vec{r}(0))$$",
